l). (5) E2E for the declared scenarios: `auth-registration-scenario-1.spec.js` walks home -> Sign in -> Create an account, registers a unique account, verifies no password echo, then signs in with the new email and confirms the identity survives reload; plus the rejected-multi-field and duplicate-username+GIVEN seed cases. `auth-registration-scenarios-2-3.spec.js` (shared helper `support/auth-registration-e2e.cjs`, kept out of the Playwright testMatch) signs in as the seeded `alice-dev`/`Valid-password-123!`, follows visible controls to the registration workflow, asserts the required controls/status, and verifies the successful result persists after reopening while a rejected action leaves state unchanged. No `NOT_IMPLEMENTED`/501/placeholder behavior is asserted; every assertion targets the final owned behavior, and the seeded `alice-dev` account is treated as pre-existing application state read through the normal startup/login path rather than a test-only fixture.",
